IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `P9-gate`

-- P9-art-85-87: Section 4 "Remedies": Article 85 "Right to lodge a complaint with a market surveillance authority",
-- Article 86 "Right to explanation of individual decision-making" and Article 87 "Reporting of infringements and protection
-- of reporting persons" (consolidated text of 27.7.2026; unchanged by the Omnibus). Group General (2 August 2026).
-- Every function takes `the date asked` first; before the group applies the answer is NOTHING (limited by its own wording).
-- A right is a grant: a function named for a right or a power answers NOTHING, not JUST FALSE, where an element of its
-- description is not met (the Guide's grant rule); JUST FALSE is kept for the text's own "no": Article 86(2) "shall not apply"
-- and Article 86(3) "only to the extent", and the exception "with the exception of systems listed under point 2".
-- The market surveillance authority is an official: no seat. The affected person and the deployer are the seats of Article 86.
-- Seams: Article 6(2) and Annex III (route of the AI system) is the keel's `route`; whether the infringement is real is not decided here.

§ `Article 85: the right to lodge a complaint`

DECLARE `Art 85 party` IS ONE OF
    `Art 85 the market surveillance authority`

DECLARE `Art 85 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 85(2) take the complaint into account for the purpose of conducting market surveillance activities and handle it in line with the dedicated procedures`

-- src:1355 | Without prejudice to other administrative or judicial remedies, any natural or legal person having grounds to consider that there has been an infringement of the provisions of this Regulation may submit complaints to the relevant market surveillance authority.
@ref Art 85(1) (src:1355)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the person is a natural or legal person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has grounds to consider that there has been an infringement of the provisions of this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 85(1) the person may submit a complaint to the relevant market surveillance authority` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that the Regulation gives no such right
    ELSE IF       `the person is a natural or legal person`
              AND `the person has grounds to consider that there has been an infringement of the provisions of this Regulation`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is to "any natural or legal person having grounds to consider that there has been an infringement"; outside that description the text neither gives nor denies the right (a grant: fork F-85-grounds)

-- "such complaints shall be taken into account ... and shall be handled in line with the dedicated procedures"
-- src:1356 | In accordance with Regulation (EU) 2019/1020, such complaints shall be taken into account for the purpose of conducting market surveillance activities, and shall be handled in line with the dedicated procedures established therefor by the market surveillance authorities.
@ref Art 85(2) (src:1356)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `a complaint has been submitted to the relevant market surveillance authority under Article 85(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 85(2) the market surveillance authority must take the complaint into account and handle it in line with the dedicated procedures` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that nothing is owed
    ELSE IF `a complaint has been submitted to the relevant market surveillance authority under Article 85(1)`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "such complaints", the complaints of paragraph 1

@ref Art 85(2)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `a complaint has been submitted to the relevant market surveillance authority under Article 85(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 85 party` `Art 85 act`
`Art 85(2) the duty of the market surveillance authority to take the complaint into account` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 85(2) the market surveillance authority must take the complaint into account and handle it in line with the dedicated procedures` `the date asked` `a complaint has been submitted to the relevant market surveillance authority under Article 85(1)`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        PARTY `Art 85 the market surveillance authority`
        MUST `Art 85(2) take the complaint into account for the purpose of conducting market surveillance activities and handle it in line with the dedicated procedures`
        HENCE FULFILLED
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

§ `Article 86: the right to explanation of individual decision-making`

DECLARE `Art 86 party` IS ONE OF
    `Art 86 the deployer`

DECLARE `Art 86 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 86(1) give the affected person clear and meaningful explanations of the role of the AI system in the decision-making procedure and the main elements of the decision taken`

-- The right, stated once; the deployer's duty (below) is the same relation seen from the deployer.
-- args: the date asked, the AI system, the decision facts, then the two exceptions of paragraphs 2 and 3.
-- src:1359 | 1. Any affected person subject to a decision which is taken by the deployer on the basis of the output from a high-risk AI system listed in Annex III, with the exception of systems listed under point 2 thereof, and which produces legal effects or similarly significantly affects that person in a way that they consider to have an adverse impact on their health, safety or fundamental rights shall have the right to obtain from the deployer clear and meaningful explanations of the role of the AI system in the decision-making procedure and the main elements of the decision taken.
@ref Art 86(1) (src:1359)
-- src:1360 | 2. Paragraph 1 shall not apply to the use of AI systems for which exceptions from, or restrictions to, the obligation under that paragraph follow from Union or national law in compliance with Union law.
@ref Art 86(2) (src:1360)
-- src:1361 | 3. This Article shall apply only to the extent that the right referred to in paragraph 1 is not otherwise provided for under Union law.
@ref Art 86(3) (src:1361)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the person is an affected person subject to a decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is taken by the deployer on the basis of the output from the AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is listed in Annex III under a point other than point 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is listed in Annex III under point 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision produces legal effects or similarly significantly affects the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person considers that the decision has an adverse impact on their health, safety or fundamental rights` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an exception or restriction follows from Union or national law in compliance with Union law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the right is otherwise provided for under Union law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 86(1) the affected person has the right to obtain from the deployer clear and meaningful explanations` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies to the AI system` `the date asked` `the AI system`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application, and Article 111(2) may save the system; before that the Regulation gives no such right
    ELSE IF NOT (`the AI system`'s `route` EQUALS `Route Article 6(2) and Annex III`)
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the right is about "a high-risk AI system listed in Annex III"; for another AI system the Article is silent (a scope limit with no "only": ruling (c) of 2026-11-05)
         ELSE IF `the AI system is listed in Annex III under point 2`
              THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "with the exception of systems listed under point 2 thereof" (read literally, a system listed under point 2 is excluded even if it is also listed under another point: fork F-86-both-points)
              ELSE IF `an exception or restriction follows from Union or national law in compliance with Union law`
                   THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "2. Paragraph 1 shall not apply to the use of AI systems for which exceptions from, or restrictions to, the obligation under that paragraph follow from Union or national law in compliance with Union law."
                   ELSE IF `the right is otherwise provided for under Union law`
                        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "3. This Article shall apply only to the extent that the right referred to in paragraph 1 is not otherwise provided for under Union law." (the whole of the right being otherwise provided for: fork F-86-3-extent)
                        ELSE IF       `the person is an affected person subject to a decision`
                                  AND `the decision is taken by the deployer on the basis of the output from the AI system`
                                  AND `the AI system is listed in Annex III under a point other than point 2`
                                  AND `the decision produces legal effects or similarly significantly affects the person`
                                  AND `the person considers that the decision has an adverse impact on their health, safety or fundamental rights`
                             THEN JUST TRUE
                             ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the right is given to "any affected person subject to a decision which is taken by the deployer on the basis of the output ... and which produces legal effects or similarly significantly affects that person in a way that they consider to have an adverse impact"; a person outside that description is neither given nor refused the right (a grant: fork F-86-elements)

-- The same relation from the deployer's side: it must give the explanations the person has the right to obtain.
@ref Art 86(1)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the person is an affected person subject to a decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is taken by the deployer on the basis of the output from the AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is listed in Annex III under a point other than point 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is listed in Annex III under point 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision produces legal effects or similarly significantly affects the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person considers that the decision has an adverse impact on their health, safety or fundamental rights` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an exception or restriction follows from Union or national law in compliance with Union law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the right is otherwise provided for under Union law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 86(1) the deployer must give the affected person clear and meaningful explanations` MEANS
    `Art 86(1) the affected person has the right to obtain from the deployer clear and meaningful explanations` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the person is an affected person subject to a decision` `the decision is taken by the deployer on the basis of the output from the AI system` `the AI system is listed in Annex III under a point other than point 2` `the AI system is listed in Annex III under point 2` `the decision produces legal effects or similarly significantly affects the person` `the person considers that the decision has an adverse impact on their health, safety or fundamental rights` `an exception or restriction follows from Union or national law in compliance with Union law` `the right is otherwise provided for under Union law`

@ref Art 86(1)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the person is an affected person subject to a decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is taken by the deployer on the basis of the output from the AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is listed in Annex III under a point other than point 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is listed in Annex III under point 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision produces legal effects or similarly significantly affects the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person considers that the decision has an adverse impact on their health, safety or fundamental rights` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an exception or restriction follows from Union or national law in compliance with Union law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the right is otherwise provided for under Union law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 86 party` `Art 86 act`
`Art 86(1) the duty of the deployer to give the affected person clear and meaningful explanations` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 86(1) the deployer must give the affected person clear and meaningful explanations` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the person is an affected person subject to a decision` `the decision is taken by the deployer on the basis of the output from the AI system` `the AI system is listed in Annex III under a point other than point 2` `the AI system is listed in Annex III under point 2` `the decision produces legal effects or similarly significantly affects the person` `the person considers that the decision has an adverse impact on their health, safety or fundamental rights` `an exception or restriction follows from Union or national law in compliance with Union law` `the right is otherwise provided for under Union law`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        PARTY `Art 86 the deployer`
        MUST `Art 86(1) give the affected person clear and meaningful explanations of the role of the AI system in the decision-making procedure and the main elements of the decision taken`
        HENCE FULFILLED
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

-- What the explanation covers: "the role of the AI system in the decision-making procedure and the main elements of the decision taken".
DECLARE `Art 86(1) explanation` IS ONE OF
    `Art 86(1) the role of the AI system in the decision-making procedure`
    `Art 86(1) the main elements of the decision taken`
    `Art 86(1) another explanation`

@ref Art 86(1)
GIVEN `the explanation` IS AN `Art 86(1) explanation`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 86(1) the explanation is within the right` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the explanation`
    WHEN `Art 86(1) the role of the AI system in the decision-making procedure` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Art 86(1) the main elements of the decision taken` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Art 86(1) another explanation` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the right is "to obtain clear and meaningful explanations of the role of the AI system ... and the main elements of the decision taken"; the text does not say whether it reaches more

§ `Article 87: reporting of infringements and protection of reporting persons`

-- src:1364 | Directive (EU) 2019/1937 shall apply to the reporting of infringements of this Regulation and the protection of persons reporting such infringements.
@ref Art 87 (src:1364)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the matter is the reporting of an infringement of this Regulation or the protection of a person reporting such an infringement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 87 Directive (EU) 2019/1937 applies to the matter` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that the Regulation does not apply the Directive
    ELSE IF `the matter is the reporting of an infringement of this Regulation or the protection of a person reporting such an infringement`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Article applies the Directive "to the reporting of infringements of this Regulation and the protection of persons reporting such infringements"; for another matter it is silent (what the Directive itself says is outside this text)
